---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import CommandBlock from "../components/CommandBlock.astro";
import { RELEASE, SITE } from "../data/site";

const installerCommand = `curl -fsS https://${SITE.domain}/install.sh | sh`;
const curlCommand = `curl -fLO \\
  '${RELEASE.baseUrl}/{SHA256SUMS,${RELEASE.archive}}'`;
const installCommand = `tar -xf ${RELEASE.archive} &&
cd ${RELEASE.archive.replace(".tar.xz", "")} &&
sudo install -Dm755 suzumushi /usr/local/bin/suzumushi &&
sudo ln -s suzumushi /usr/local/bin/suzu`;
const nixCommand = `nix --extra-experimental-features 'nix-command flakes' \\
  profile add ${SITE.nixFlake}`;
---

<Layout title="Install" description="Install Suzumushi on Linux and set up your first local audio library.">
  <section class="page-head shell">
    <h1 class="display">Install Suzumushi.</h1>
    <p>Run the installer on any x86-64 GNU/Linux system, or choose the AUR package for Arch Linux or the flake for NixOS. Then create your library below. The current release is version {SITE.version}.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="shell">
    <section class="entry" aria-labelledby="installer-title">
      <h2 id="installer-title" class="title">Any x86-64 Linux</h2>
      <div class="stack">
        <p>Paste this into your terminal. It installs <code>suzumushi</code> and the <code>suzu</code> shortcut in <code>~/.local/bin</code> without sudo.</p>
        <CommandBlock command={installerCommand} label="Install" />
        <p class="small">The script installs the v{SITE.version} archive only after it matches the SHA-256 recorded in the script, and only if the player starts. If the download stops partway, nothing runs. The player needs the ALSA, PipeWire, and D-Bus libraries that most desktops already include. This site serves an exact copy of the release's <a href={`${RELEASE.baseUrl}/install.sh`}>install.sh</a>, SHA-256 <code>{RELEASE.installerChecksum}</code>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="entry" aria-labelledby="arch-title">
      <h2 id="arch-title" class="title">Arch Linux</h2>
      <div class="stack">
        <p>Install the AUR package with yay. Both <code>suzumushi</code> and <code>suzu</code> launch the player.</p>
        <CommandBlock command="yay -S suzumushi-bin" label="Install with yay" />
        <p class="small"><a href={SITE.aur} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">AUR package</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="nixos" class="entry" aria-labelledby="nixos-title">
      <h2 id="nixos-title" class="title">NixOS x86-64</h2>
      <div class="stack">
        <p>With Nix installed, add the flake to your user profile. Both <code>suzumushi</code> and <code>suzu</code> launch the player.</p>
        <CommandBlock command={nixCommand} label="Install with Nix" />
        <p class="small">Nix builds the stable v{SITE.version} release with pinned dependencies. The first installation may take a few minutes.</p>
        <p class="small"><a href={SITE.nixDocs} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">NixOS and Home Manager configuration</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="entry" aria-labelledby="by-hand-title">
      <h2 id="by-hand-title" class="title">By hand</h2>
      <div class="stack">
        <p>Download the release archive, verify its checksum, and install the player yourself.</p>
        <details>
          <summary>Show archive installation steps</summary>
          <ol class="stack hand-steps">
            <li>
              <h3 class="title">Download</h3>
              <CommandBlock command={curlCommand} label="Download" />
            </li>
            <li>
              <h3 class="title">Verify</h3>
              <CommandBlock command="sha256sum --check --ignore-missing SHA256SUMS" label="Verify" />
              <p class="small">Continue only if the archive reports <code>OK</code>. If verification fails, stop and download the files again.</p>
              <p class="small">Expected SHA-256 for v{SITE.version}: <code>{RELEASE.checksum}</code></p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h3 class="title">Install</h3>
              <CommandBlock command={installCommand} label="Install" />
            </li>
          </ol>
        </details>
        <p class="small"><a href={SITE.release} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Release files</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section id="first-library" class="library shell" aria-labelledby="first-library-title">
    <h2 id="first-library-title" class="display">Set up your first library.</h2>
    <p class="measure">Run these commands from the folder where you want to keep your Suzumushi library. The player reads audio inside that library; it doesn't automatically scan your Music folder.</p>

    <ol class="library-steps">
      <li class="entry">
        <h3 class="title"><span class="mono brass step-number" aria-hidden="true">1</span>Create your library</h3>
        <CommandBlock command="suzumushi init ./suzumushi" label="Create library" />
      </li>
      <li class="entry">
        <h3 class="title"><span class="mono brass step-number" aria-hidden="true">2</span>Add your music</h3>
        <p>In your file manager, copy audio files or folders into <code>./suzumushi/audio/library/</code>. You can keep your artist and album folders.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="entry">
        <h3 class="title"><span class="mono brass step-number" aria-hidden="true">3</span>Open the player</h3>
        <div class="stack">
          <CommandBlock command="suzumushi --root ./suzumushi" label="Start listening" />
          <p>Select a track in Library and press <kbd>Enter</kbd> to add it and start playback. Use <kbd>Space</kbd> to pause and <kbd>?</kbd> for the key guide.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <div class="shell">
    <section class="entry" aria-labelledby="audio-title">
      <h2 id="audio-title" class="title">Audio support</h2>
      <div class="stack">
        <p>The verified formats are MP3, FLAC, signed 16-bit PCM WAV, and Ogg Vorbis. Mono and stereo audio from 8 kHz through 192 kHz is supported when the default device accepts the source rate.</p>
        <p>AAC, M4A, Opus, multichannel audio, and automatic resampling are not included in verified support.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="entry" aria-labelledby="source-title">
      <h2 id="source-title" class="title">Build from source</h2>
      <div class="stack">
        <p>You need Rust 1.95 or newer and the development packages for your distribution.</p>
        <details>
          <summary>Show build steps</summary>
          <div class="stack hand-steps">
            <ul>
              <li>Arch Linux: <code>alsa-lib dbus pipewire clang pkgconf</code></li>
              <li>Debian or Ubuntu: <code>libasound2-dev libpipewire-0.3-dev libspa-0.2-dev libdbus-1-dev libclang-dev pkg-config</code></li>
              <li>Fedora: <code>alsa-lib-devel pipewire-devel dbus-devel libclang-devel pkgconf-pkg-config</code></li>
            </ul>
            <CommandBlock command={`git clone https://github.com/nuggocto/suzumushi.git &&\ncd suzumushi &&\ncargo install --path . --locked`} label="Build and install" />
            <p>After installation, follow the <a href="#first-library">library setup instructions</a> above.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <p class="small"><a href="/">Back to the player</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .library {
    padding-block: 4rem 2rem;
  }

  .library > p {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
  }

  .library-steps {
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .library-steps .entry {
    padding-block: 1.25rem;
  }

  .step-number {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 2rem;
  }

  .hand-steps {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  ol.hand-steps li + li {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .library {
      padding-block: 6rem 3rem;
    }

    /* A command's first line sits on the same baseline as the title beside it. */
    .library-steps .entry > :global(.command),
    .library-steps .entry > .stack {
      margin-top: -0.45rem;
    }
  }
</style>
